  {
   "id": 2,
   "ref": "600–603",
   "en": "Could I not have seized his body and torn it apart, scattered it on the waves? Could I not have put his men to the sword — Ascanius himself — and [served him up|17,18] at his own father's table? True, the fortune of that fight would have been uncertain. So be it —",
   "en_marked": "[Could I|2] [not|1] have [seized|3] his [body|5] [and|6] [torn it apart|4], [scattered it|8] [on the waves|7]? [Could I|2] [not|9] have [put|13] his [men|10] [to the sword|14] — [Ascanius|15] [himself|12] — [and|16] [served him up|17,18] at his {own|Not in the Latin. Added to stress the horror of serving a son at his father's table.} [father's|16] [table|19]? [True|20], the [fortune|24] of that [fight|22] [would have been|23] [uncertain|21]. [So be it|25] —",
